{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"gpuType":"T4","authorship_tag":"ABX9TyNy7wiJJXB7VvZ3pP/oGTEc"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"},"accelerator":"GPU"},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Image preprocessing"],"metadata":{"id":"gd9vFY2sMXwW"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Image processing is divided into analogue image processing and digital image processing.\n","\n","Digital image processing is the use of computer algorithms to perform image processing on digital images. It allows a much wider range of algorithms to be applied to the input data - the aim of digital image processing is to improve the image data (features) by suppressing unwanted distortions and/or enhancement of some important image features so that our AI models can benefit from this improved data to work on.\n","\n","Are Black and White and Grayscale images the same?\n","\n","Black and white (monochrome),has only two \"colors\", black (ink or toner) and white (no ink or toner). It is used for things like text, where you want everything that is a printed character to be black and the background white.\n","\n","Grayscale contains shades of grey and is used for reproducing images.\n","\n","So most of the images you see are actually grayscale."],"metadata":{"id":"D_xSLQPzMbVe"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Introduction"],"metadata":{"id":"eNoJgklNMhWy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["In this tutorial, we will be working around an image of a penguin. You can download it from here:\n","\n","https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/images/g_disneynaturepenguins_01_17789_d494d9a3.jpeg?region=0%2C0%2C1200%2C560&width=1136"],"metadata":{"id":"sw0eeMhHMmxf"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Basic Operations with OpenCV"],"metadata":{"id":"BbUCp-eaMqpr"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Importing OpenCV\n","The first requirement is to import the OpenCV module."],"metadata":{"i